  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA containing NNN elements. Count the number of positive integers XXX satisfying the following condition :\n\n\n(X⊕Ai)&lt;Ai(X \\oplus A_i) &lt; A_i(X⊕Ai​)&lt;Ai​ for all 1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N, where ⊕\\oplus⊕ represents the Bitwise XOR operator.\nIt can be proven that the answer is always finite under the given constraints.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line contains NNN - the size of the array\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,...,ANA_1, A_2, ..., A_NA1​,A2​,...,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the number of valid positive integers XXX.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Ai&lt;2301 \\le A_i \\lt 2^{30}1≤Ai​&lt;230",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n2\n1 3\n4\n10 3 5 18\n1\n5",
        "output": "1\n0\n5",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest 1 : The only number satisfying the constraint is 111.\n\n1⊕1=0<11 \\oplus 1 = 0 < 11⊕1=0<1\n1⊕3=2<31 \\oplus 3 = 2 < 31⊕3=2<3\n\nTest Case 2 : It can be proven that there is no valid number."
      }
    ]
  },
